            3
          ],
          "caption": "Table 1. Features of systems providing privacy for agentic AI (example systems in parentheses). Like other IFC systems, GAAP provides data disclosure guarantees (f1), and does so deterministically (unlike model-generated policies ). GAAP does not rely on trusted data and trust labels (f2), unlike existing IFC and policy systems that aim for integrity and need to ensure only trusted data can influence control flow. Furthermore, GAAP’s confidentiality guarantees do not rely on any trusted model (f3), unlike systems that need trusted models to generate code or policies to restrict control flow. GAAP also builds the user’s data disclosure policy over time (f4), persists it across tasks (f5), and supports multi-shot executions (taints across LLM calls) (f6).",
